[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. The reports in it say otherwise.
Read by what each report describes and by the tenant it came from, #4471 holds three problems.
Each now has its own ticket, with the count of reports it covers.

<Callout kind="warn">
Shipping the parser fix closes the biggest group only. The other two keep coming in.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} repo="adrianoresende/mega-s01e03-support-kb" />

1. **`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** A day-first tenant's
   `5/3` becomes 3 May. This is the fix that is queued.
2. **`hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** People at day-first
   tenants on booking-v3 (Alder Physio, Copper Studio, Pale Harbour) type what the hint says,
   and the form reads it the tenant's way. Only reports that came in through the form. The
   parser fix does not touch it: the hint is wrong, not the parser.
3. **`shift`: invites land one day off.** "Tuesday 12 May, calendar says Monday 11 May";
   "Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday"; "the invite arrived before I made the booking".
   No day and month swap explains these. It is a time-zone or DST conversion bug. The desk
   read them that way already (desk-notes), but filed them under `parser` by tenant.

## How the counts were made

- **One id, one report.** The export pages overlap, so some reports are in it twice. The count is over unique ids.
- **By tenant, not by intake tag.** `intakeTag` is intake's guess from the reporter's browser.
  The cause depends on the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), and the two disagree.
- **By what the report says.** Every other report names two dates that are the same day and
  month swapped. The `shift` reports do not.

## What the old page showed

The table on #4471, for comparison. It puts `hint` in red with no ticket, and folds the
one-day moves into `parser` as a footnote.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes on the desk

- Matching on subject (decision 0001) merged these: the same subjects came in for all three
  problems. Splitting needs the tenant and the body, not the subject.
- Close #4471 against the `parser` ticket only, and keep the other two open after the fix ships.

